#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The per-commit matrix: one commit's checks on every lab GPU, lavapipe and the Windows host,
run through potluck, with the results attached to the commit as a git note
(refs/notes/matrix, one JSON document per commit; local, never pushed).

    scripts/matrix/matrix run [SHA] [--legs LEG,...] [--dry-run]
    scripts/matrix/matrix show [SHA]

SHA defaults to development's tip. Both print each leg's verdict line, then every harness row's
time and GPU time on both runtimes, with the old runtime's move on the leg's base, and the rows
that move voids (results.harness_rows, results.FROZEN_DRIFT). A leg is a GPU, named by its PCI
vendor:device (`1002:744c`), or `lavapipe`. docs/VALIDATION.md ("The matrix") has the legs, the
records and the rules; CONTRIBUTING.md has how to run it.

The cluster's own facts come from potluck (its nodes, their GPUs and CPUs) and from
~/.config/metal2vulkan/matrix.json:

    {"builders": [{"node": "A", "gate": "SHELL COMMAND", "portable": true}, {"node": "B"}],
     "setup": {"A": "SHELL"},
     "skip_gpus": ["vendor:device"],
     "record_nodes": {"vendor:device": "A"},
     "validation_layer": "PATH"}

The first builder whose gate command exits 0 (no gate: always) builds the GPU legs' test archive
and runs the lavapipe leg. Its archive runs on every Linux node when it is `portable`, else only
on nodes of its CPU model; any other node builds its own. `setup` is shell each job on that node
runs first. A GPU in `skip_gpus` gets no leg. A card in `record_nodes` has its leg of record on
that node, named by the card, and runs as an extra leg, `vendor:device@node`, on each other node
that holds it, judged like any leg. `validation_layer` is the carry
`scripts/validation-layer make` made (default ~/.cache/metal2vulkan-matrix/validation-layer):
every job that runs rt's device tests (each GPU leg's, lavapipe's, the Windows host's) unpacks
its OS's directory in its workspace and points the loader at it, and its note gives the layer's
version (`layer`); the harness's timing jobs run without it.
"""

